      "writtenOn": "2026-06-09T23:09:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason is that they are not necessarily tightly coupled. `compileContainer` refers to the container in which the guest test are compiled. `hostContainer` refers to the container in which the guest VM will be running from when running guest tests. Technically they don\u0027t have to be the same as there\u0027s no connection between the two (You could for example **compile** the guest tests in ubuntu 14.04, but run a guest VM based on a 14.04 (qemu)image from a 26.04 host docker container)\n\nEssentially there are three components to guest tests:\n1. Which (docker container) version they are compiled in? [compileContainer]\n2. Which (qemu VM) version they are running in? (should be the same version as 1, but as a qemu image instead of docker) [guestVMImage]\n3. Which docker container version the qemu VM is running from. [hostContainer]",
